{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"spectralOrdering"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"normalized"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":" = false, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"tolerance"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1e-8, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"maxIterations"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"NoConvergence","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"] "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SB","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BinaryFloatingPoint"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full reorthogonalization, the null space projected"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, from a fixed start vector: on σI − L (σ twice the largest weighted degree; 2I − N with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"normalized","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") while σ\/λ₂ is moderate, else on L⁺ by shift-invert, each product a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conjugate-gradient solve with L grounded at the vertex of largest degree. A Ritz pair is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accepted when its residual is at most "},{"code":"tolerance","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" · λ₂, so λ₂ is relative to itself however"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the weights spread; the value is then the vector’s Rayleigh quotient, a sum over edges. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dense solver below 64 vertices. O((n + m) · products) time; 31 n "},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s (34 n from 5,000"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices, for the polynomial filter), and on the shift-invert path O(n + m) more for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"solver."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position; a weight of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"0 is no edge."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","name":"Precondition","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance > 0"},{"text":". Every weight is finite and nonnegative, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"text":", when given, is at least 1.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"},{"style":"note","name":"Throws","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoConvergence"},{"text":" when the Lanczos run on L⁺ spends ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"text":" matrix–vector","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"products (1,000 when nil) without converging, with the products spent and the Ritz","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"residual relative to 1\/λ₂. The run on σI − L that may come first hands over to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shift-invert rather than throwing, after 4,000 + 20√n products or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whichever is smaller. Each shift-invert product is a conjugate-gradient solve that throws,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with its own iterations and relative residual, after 20,000 + 2n. Below 64 vertices the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dense solver answers and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"text":" is unused. Only a tolerance below rounding has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reached the default limits in the measurements.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside"}]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P08SpectralA6TheoryE16spectralOrdering6weight10normalized9tolerance13maxIterationsSay6VertexQzGqd__5Edges_5IndexQZXE_SbSdSiSgtAA13NoConvergenceVYKSBRd__lF","roleHeading":"Instance Method","title":"spectralOrdering(weight:normalized:tolerance:maxIterations:)","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"spectralOrdering","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"normalized"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"tolerance"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"maxIterations"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":"?) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV","text":"NoConvergence"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpectralGraphTheory\/FiedlerVector.swift#L380","fileName":"FiedlerVector.swift"},"modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"SpectralGraphTheory"}],"symbolKind":"method","role":"symbol"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/spectralOrdering(weight:normalized:tolerance:maxIterations:)-4aqxc","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/spectralordering(weight:normalized:tolerance:maxiterations:)-4aqxc"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The spectral ordering (NetworkX "},{"code":"spectral_ordering","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; Barnard, Pothen and Simon): the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"components in order of their least vertex index; a component of at most two vertices in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index order; a larger one ascending by the Fiedler vector of that component (for a connected"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph, "},{"code":"fiedlerVector()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s), entries within 10⁻⁸ · max|x| of their predecessor kept in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index order. "},{"code":"[]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for the empty graph."}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory":{"title":"SpectralGraphTheory","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory","abstract":[],"role":"collection"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/NoConvergence":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NoConvergence"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"NoConvergence","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NoConvergence"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/noconvergence","abstract":[{"text":"The error an iterative method throws when it spends its iteration limit without meeting its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stopping rule: a power iteration (eigenvector and Katz centrality, PageRank, HITS), a Lanczos","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or conjugate-gradient run, or a QL eigenvalue iteration. Named after Eigen’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"ComputationInfo::NoConvergence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; NetworkX raises ","type":"text"},{"code":"PowerIterationFailedConvergence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and SciPy","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"ArpackNoConvergence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the same place.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Edges-swift.associatedtype":{"abstract":[],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"associatedtype","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Collection","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl"}],"title":"Edges","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph\/edges-swift.associatedtype","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols":{"abstract":[],"role":"collection","title":"GraphProtocols","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Graph","kind":"symbol","navigatorT